        "dash": "solid",
        "size": "s",
        "font": "sans",
        "text": "CURRENT ARCHITECTURE CONSTRAINTS\n\nNotionPageReference validates Notion-only hosts and extracts a 32-char hex page ID.\nNotionWebNavigationPolicy blocks all non-Notion navigation (opens in system browser).\nNotionWebSession injects Notion-specific JS (selection capture, quick copy, scroll restoration) on a single WKWebView.\nPinnedPageModel (SwiftData) already stores canonicalURL generically, but the domain layer is Notion-specific.\nPiPRecentPagesShelfView + Controller already provide page switching — the natural 'switch back to Notion' mechanism.\n\nGOAL: Let users pin arbitrary HTTPS URLs (e.g., Canvas) as a beta feature, with easy switching back to Notion pages.",
        "align": "middle",
        "verticalAlign": "middle",
        "growY": 0,
        "url": ""
      },
      "index": "a3",
      "parentId": "page:page"
    },
    {
      "id": "shape:a1-header",
      "typeName": "shape",
      "type": "geo",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 230,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "props": {
        "w": 680,
        "h": 45,
        "geo": "rectangle",
        "color": "violet",
        "labelColor": "white",
        "fill": "solid",
        "dash": "solid",
        "size": "m",
        "font": "sans",
        "text": "1. Generalize NotionPageReference → PinnedPageReference",
        "align": "middle",
        "verticalAlign": "middle",
        "growY": 0,
        "url": ""
      },
      "index": "a4",
      "parentId": "page:page"
    },
    {
      "id": "shape:a1-body",
      "typeName": "shape",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10,
      "y": 285,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "props": {
        "text": "Rename NotionPageReference to PinnedPageReference. Make host validation optional — Notion URLs extract the page ID as today; other HTTPS URLs use the URL or a hash as the identifier.\n\nPROS\n✓ Single unified type flows through all code paths\n✓ Recent pages shelf works unchanged\n✓ No parallel code paths to maintain\n✓ Natural switching between Notion and external\n\nCONS\n✗ Massive refactor — NotionPageReference is referenced everywhere\n✗ Page ID extraction is Notion-specific\n✗ Selection capture, quick copy, scroll restore all break\n✗ High risk to existing Notion behavior\n✗ Title suffix stripping ('| Notion') needs special casing\n\nKEY FILES: NotionPageReference.swift, PageRepository.swift, NotionWebSession.swift, WebNavigationDestination.swift, NotionWebNavigationPolicy.swift, PiPPanelCoordinator.swift, AppRuntime.swift, PinCoordinator.swift, ExternalURLRoute.swift + all tests\n\nSWITCH BACK: Recent pages shelf lists all pinned pages — selecting a Notion page restores the full experience.",
        "size": "s",
        "font": "sans",
        "align": "start",
        "w": 660,
        "autoSize": false
      },
      "index": "a5",
      "parentId": "page:page"
    },
    {
      "id": "shape:a2-header",
      "typeName": "shape",
      "type": "geo",
      "x": 700,
      "y": 230,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "props": {
        "w": 680,
        "h": 45,
        "geo": "rectangle",
        "color": "green",
        "labelColor": "white",
        "fill": "solid",
        "dash": "solid",
        "size": "m",
        "font": "sans",
        "text": "2. Parallel PinnedPage enum  ←  RECOMMENDED",
        "align": "middle",
        "verticalAlign": "middle",
        "growY": 0,
        "url": ""
      },
      "index": "a6",
      "parentId": "page:page"
    },
    {
      "id": "shape:a2-body",
      "typeName": "shape",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 710,
      "y": 285,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "props": {
        "text": "Keep NotionPageReference untouched. Add:\n  enum PinnedPage { case notion(NotionPageReference); case web(URL, String?) }\nThe panel and web session accept PinnedPage. Notion path runs existing logic; web path loads the URL generically.\n\nPROS\n✓ Zero risk to existing Notion behavior\n✓ Clear separation of concerns\n✓ Beta-gatable behind a feature flag\n✓ Notion features (selection, quick copy) stay Notion-only\n✓ Gradual migration possible\n✓ PinnedPageModel already stores URL generically\n\nCONS\n✗ Two code paths in web session + coordinator\n✗ Must thread PinnedPage through PiPPanelCoordinating\n✗ New schema migration (add 'kind' field)\n✗ More types to test\n\nKEY FILES: new PinnedPage.swift, PiPPanelCoordinator.swift, NotionWebSession.swift, PinCoordinator.swift, PageRepository.swift, PinnedPageModel.swift, PerchSchema.swift (V6), WebNavigationDestination.swift, SettingsView.swift\n\nSWITCH BACK: Recent pages shelf shows both types. Selecting a Notion page restores full Notion experience — selection capture, quick copy, scroll restore all reactivate.",
        "size": "s",
        "font": "sans",
        "align": "start",
        "w": 660,
        "autoSize": false
      },
      "index": "a7",
      "parentId": "page:page"
    },
    {
      "id": "shape:a3-header",
      "typeName": "shape",
      "type": "geo",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 730,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "props": {
        "w": 680,
