        "dash": "solid",
        "size": "m",
        "font": "sans",
        "text": "3. Multi-WebView tabs",
        "align": "middle",
        "verticalAlign": "middle",
        "growY": 0,
        "url": ""
      },
      "index": "a8",
      "parentId": "page:page"
    },
    {
      "id": "shape:a3-body",
      "typeName": "shape",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10,
      "y": 785,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "props": {
        "text": "Web session maintains a pool of WKWebViews — one per pinned page. Switching shows/hides the corresponding view, configured for its domain.\n\nPROS\n✓ Instant switching — no reloads\n✓ Full state preserved (scroll, forms, JS state)\n✓ Natural 'multiple apps' model\n✓ Each view configured independently\n\nCONS\n✗ Memory cost — each WKWebView is heavy\n✗ WebKit process limit (~10 views)\n✗ NotionWebLifecycleController deeply tied to single view\n✗ Major refactor of suspend / resume / evict\n✗ Panel geometry and animation assume single view\n\nKEY FILES: NotionWebSession.swift (major), NotionWebLifecycleController.swift (major), PiPChromeView.swift, PiPPanelCoordinator.swift + new view pool manager\n\nSWITCH BACK: Each pinned page has its own live web view — like browser tabs. No reload needed.",
        "size": "s",
        "font": "sans",
        "align": "start",
        "w": 660,
        "autoSize": false
      },
      "index": "a9",
      "parentId": "page:page"
    },
    {
      "id": "shape:a4-header",
