    },
    {
      "id": "shape:rec-body",
      "typeName": "shape",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 710,
      "y": 1305,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "props": {
        "text": "RATIONALE\n• Lowest risk to existing Notion behavior — NotionPageReference stays untouched\n• Beta-gatable behind a feature flag in Settings\n• Recent pages shelf already provides 'switch back to Notion' — no new UI needed\n• PinnedPageModel stores URL generically — just add a 'kind' field\n• NotionWebSession already loads URLs via loadRequest; Notion-specific JS can be conditionally skipped\n• WebNavigationDestination already distinguishes .trustedNotion from .externalWeb\n• Gradual: start with URL loading, add features over time\n\nMIGRATION: Add PinnedPageSchemaV6 with optional 'kind' field (default: 'notion'). Lightweight migration. Existing rows default to notion kind.\n\nBETA GATE: Settings toggle 'Allow non-Notion URLs (Beta)'. Off by default. When on, PageURLInputView accepts any HTTPS URL instead of only Notion hosts.\n\nNAVIGATION: WebNavigationDestination.classify needs to allow the pinned external URL. The policy allows navigation to a pinned external URL but still opens other external links in the system browser.",
        "size": "s",
        "font": "sans",
        "align": "start",
        "w": 660,
        "autoSize": false
      },
      "index": "b6",
      "parentId": "page:page"
    },
    {
      "id": "shape:flow-header",
      "typeName": "shape",
      "type": "geo",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1790,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "props": {
        "w": 1400,
        "h": 40,
        "geo": "rectangle",
        "color": "grey",
        "labelColor": "black",
        "fill": "semi",
        "dash": "solid",
        "size": "m",
        "font": "sans",
        "text": "Data flow for recommended approach",
        "align": "middle",
        "verticalAlign": "middle",
        "growY": 0,
        "url": ""
      },
      "index": "b7",
      "parentId": "page:page"
    },
    {
      "id": "shape:flow-body",
      "typeName": "shape",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10,
      "y": 1842,
      "rotation": 0,
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "props": {
        "text": "User pastes URL → PinCoordinator.page(from:) → validates as NotionPageReference OR creates PinnedPage.web(url)\n→ PiPPanelCoordinator.show(page: PinnedPage) → NotionWebSession.activate(page: PinnedPage)\n→ If .notion: inject Notion JS, enable selection capture, quick copy, scroll restore\n→ If .web: load URL with generic WKWebView config, skip Notion-specific JS\n→ PageRepository.recordVisit(PinnedPage) → stores kind + URL + title\n→ Recent pages shelf shows both types → user selects Notion page → full Notion experience restored\n\nKEY DECISION: WebNavigationDestination.classify gets a new .pinnedExternal case (or reuses .externalWeb with a check against the pinned URL set). The navigation policy allows navigation to the pinned external URL but still opens other external links in the system browser.\n\nEXISTING HOOKS: ExternalURLRoute already parses perch://pin?url=... — this can be extended to accept non-Notion URLs when the beta flag is on. The PiPRecentPagesShelfController.selection(for:) method already reconstructs a NotionPageReference from a StoredPageSnapshot; it would also handle PinnedPage.web.",
        "size": "s",
        "font": "sans",
        "align": "start",
        "w": 1380,
        "autoSize": false
      },
      "index": "b8",
      "parentId": "page:page"
    }
